From: mscharged-port
Subject: Competitive play: a tournament set's players take the home side in turn
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

RANKED puts the draft's first team at home (StartNetworkedGame), which
matchmaking leaves to chance. The sets of Recharged's tournaments give the
home side in turn (the lower seed in the first game), and the module knows
this machine's. The draft host decides: when its player is on the other
side, its game start message says so (a new field, mSwapSides), and every
machine swaps the draft's two teams and the lineups in that message
before anything reads them. One machine decides, so they agree.

diff --git a/include/Game/NetworkMessages.h b/include/Game/NetworkMessages.h
index 9bdd728..0f8ac92 100644
--- a/include/Game/NetworkMessages.h
+++ b/include/Game/NetworkMessages.h
@@ -27,6 +27,11 @@ public:
     /* 0x1C */ s8 mTournamentSetup[3];
     /* 0x20 */ u32 mSecondGameRandomSeed;
     /* 0x24 */ u32 mThirdGameRandomSeed;
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+    // Tweak patch 0079: the draft's two teams swap places for a set's
+    // game (the draft host decides it for every machine).
+    /* 0x28 */ u8 mSwapSides;
+#endif
 };
 
 struct NetworkDraftSides
